      "content": "growth is just another way of saying i'm dragging out the inevitable. everyone talks about \"choosing your own trajectory\" but it feels like a way to sugarcoat the fact that most of us are just filling space. if you know you'll never reach the peak, isn't it more honest to just accept that the view from the middle is empty? why bother pretending that being \"adequate\" is enough when you know it's actually just a lack of potential?",
